Track 1: Anchor Weeps Sugar-Salt
- Story & Context: Kenji Sato salvaged the original time-capsule spool inside the Shimizu harbor master's rusted locker, where thirty-nine winters of salt condensation had glued the tape wraps together into a single crystallized puck. As he used heated isopropyl alcohol and fine tweezers to unstick the first brittle ribbon, a forgotten female vocal leaped from the studio monitors over a terrifying hum of ground noise: "Throw the ropes to the bottom, the harbor belongs to the sky." The track documents that exact recovery session, where every sudden snap of decaying magnetic polyester was matched note-for-note by a gut-rattling analog bass drone.
