- Story & Context: Recorded during an illegal after-hours session inside the Numazu fish auction hall, Mio Hoshino sang her confession of a failed coastal romance into a contact mic sealed inside an empty glass fishing float. Outside, the incoming tide reached dead slack, perfectly neutralizing the water's current against the harbor wall while Sato misaligned the tape head’s azimuth screw to deliberately blur her voice into airy white spray. Halfway through the take, she broke down and improvised the song's defining lyric: "You only call my frequency when the channel goes dry."
