- Story & Context: Local myth claims that during the final playback of this song at the Miho lighthouse, the building’s foundations vibrated with such low-frequency resonance that schools of deep-sea lanternfish beached themselves along the sandbar. Rei Hoshino tracked the lead vocal in a single continuous breath while watching local fisherman drag an unregistered radio transponder out of the black water. The track ends on a loop of decaying synthesizer chime and a haunting chant: "Leave the lights untied, nobody is sailing home tonight."
